# text = Her daughter , Miss de Bourgh , will have a very large fortune , and it is believed that she and her cousin will unite the two estates Mr . Collins speaks highly both of Lady Catherine and her daughter ; but from some particulars that he has related of her ladyship , I suspect his gratitude misleads him , and that in spite of her being his patroness , she is an arrogant , conceited woman I believe her to be both in a great degree I have not seen her for many years , but I very well remember that I never liked her , and that her manners were dictatorial and insolent .
